{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Her hand</b> — two instances in the Masorah: one is דין (judgment) and the other כפה פרשה לעני (her hand, the section about the poor). Just as there it concerns money, so here too money." "<b>Your eye</b> — adjacent to it: לא יהיה לך בכיסך (you shall not have in your pouch). This teaches not to look at the pouch, at his private parts and his nakedness. Another interpretation: עינך לא יהיה לך בכיסך (your eye shall not be in your pouch) — to count what is in it, for blessing is found only in a thing hidden from the eye." "<b>And you shall cut off her hand</b> — adjacent to it: לא יהיה לך בכיסך (you shall not have in your pouch). This teaches that וקצותה את כפה (and you shall cut off her hand) is monetary, a matter placed in the pouch."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:40.882807447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}